# React Rules

## Components

- Function declarations only: `function ComponentName()`. No arrow functions.
- Named exports. No `default export` for components.
- No `React.FC`.
- Props interface: `ComponentNameProps`.
- Max ~150 lines per component. Extract sub-components when growing.

## State

- Avoid `useState` for derived values. Calculate them.
- Avoid `useEffect` for state sync. Derive instead.
- Local state only for UI concerns (open/closed, selected tab, form input).

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
const [filtered, setFiltered] = useState([]);
useEffect(() => { setFiltered(items.filter(...)) }, [items]);

// ✅ Good
const filtered = items.filter(...);
```

## Effects

`useEffect` is for external system synchronization ONLY:
- Browser API subscriptions (resize, media queries)
- Third-party widget sync
- DOM cleanup

NOT for: derived state, data fetching, state synchronization.

## Memoization

- Do NOT use `useMemo`/`useCallback` by default.
- Only when there is a measured performance problem.

## Forms

- React Hook Form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod`.
- Zod schema defines validation.
- Submit calls Server Action.
- Reset on success. Preserve on validation error.

## Hooks

- Custom hooks: `use` prefix, camelCase.
- Location: `src/features/[feature]/hooks/` or `src/lib/hooks/`.
- No business logic in hooks.

## Composition

- Pages compose feature components.
- Feature components compose shared/UI components.
- Avoid prop drilling. Use composition or context sparingly.

See `docs/coding-conventions.md` for full details.